  "description": "The 2026 general election for Pennsylvania's 12th Congressional District pits incumbent Democrat Summer Lee against Republican James Hayes. The district encompasses most of Pittsburgh and its eastern suburbs, including parts of Allegheny and Westmoreland counties. Lee, a progressive member of 'The Squad' first elected in 2022 and now seeking her third term, won the Democratic primary on May 19, 2026 with 81.2% of the vote against challenger William Parker. Hayes, a business executive and economist, ran unopposed for the Republican nomination. Cook Political Report rates the race as 'Solid Democratic,' as the district has a D+19.2% Cook Partisan Voting Index, though national midterm dynamics could affect turnout.",
